// grmb design corpus. Hand-written against docs/design/grmb-spec.md (cycle 1
// grammar); NOT machine-checked (the P1 parser predates cycle 1). Findings below
// are what the rules of that file predict, to be confirmed by P0/P1.
// Stress 2: an externally owned open outcome set gains a code
//
// EXPECTED FINDINGS
//   As written: no MDL022 or MDL032 (every known variant has an arm; open set)
//   New code upstream that no variant models: PLAN011 (once bound to code),
//   detail naming the unknown arm that receives it (PLAN017 retired, D193)
//   Without an unknown arm: MDL033
// NOT EXPRESSIBLE (open questions: docs/design/grmb-spec.md 19)

step system.charge : open { ok, declined, expired };
scenario pay realizes buyer.pay {
  buyer.pays -> system.charge => { ok => end ok; declined => end err(declined); expired => end err(expired); unknown => end err(declined); }
}
// then add `stolen_card` upstream: PLAN011 (detail: the unknown arm)
